#: ../../source/powerpoint_SKILL.md:51
msgid "Design Ideas"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/powerpoint_SKILL.md:53
msgid ""
"**Don't create boring slides.** Plain bullets on a white background won't"
" impress anyone. Consider ideas from this list for each slide."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/powerpoint_SKILL.md:55
msgid "Before Starting"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/powerpoint_SKILL.md:57
msgid ""
"**Pick a bold, content-informed color palette**: The palette should feel "
"designed for THIS topic. If swapping your colors into a completely "
"different presentation would still \"work,\" you haven't made specific "
"enough choices."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/powerpoint_SKILL.md:58
msgid ""
"**Dominance over equality**: One color should dominate (60-70% visual "
"weight), with 1-2 supporting tones and one sharp accent. Never give all "
"colors equal weight."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/powerpoint_SKILL.md:59
msgid ""
"**Dark/light contrast**: Dark backgrounds for title + conclusion slides, "
"light for content (\"sandwich\" structure). Or commit to dark throughout "
"for a premium feel."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/powerpoint_SKILL.md:60
msgid ""
"**Commit to a visual motif**: Pick ONE distinctive element and repeat it "
"— rounded image frames, icons in colored circles, thick single-side "
"borders. Carry it across every slide."
msgstr ""

