msgid "0.3-0.5\" between content blocks"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/powerpoint_SKILL.md:124
msgid "Leave breathing room—don't fill every inch"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/powerpoint_SKILL.md:126
msgid "Avoid (Common Mistakes)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/powerpoint_SKILL.md:128
msgid ""
"**Don't repeat the same layout** — vary columns, cards, and callouts "
"across slides"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/powerpoint_SKILL.md:129
msgid ""
"**Don't center body text** — left-align paragraphs and lists; center only"
" titles"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/powerpoint_SKILL.md:130
msgid ""
"**Don't skimp on size contrast** — titles need 36pt+ to stand out from "
"14-16pt body"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/powerpoint_SKILL.md:131
msgid "**Don't default to blue** — pick colors that reflect the specific topic"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/powerpoint_SKILL.md:132
msgid ""
"**Don't mix spacing randomly** — choose 0.3\" or 0.5\" gaps and use "
"consistently"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/powerpoint_SKILL.md:133
msgid ""
"**Don't style one slide and leave the rest plain** — commit fully or keep"
" it simple throughout"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/powerpoint_SKILL.md:134
msgid ""
"**Don't create text-only slides** — add images, icons, charts, or visual "
"elements; avoid plain title + bullets"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/powerpoint_SKILL.md:135
msgid ""
"**Don't forget text box padding** — when aligning lines or shapes with "
"text edges, set `margin: 0` on the text box or offset the shape to "
"account for padding"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/powerpoint_SKILL.md:136
msgid ""
"**Don't use low-contrast elements** — icons AND text need strong contrast"
" against the background; avoid light text on light backgrounds or dark "
"text on dark backgrounds"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/powerpoint_SKILL.md:137
msgid ""
"**NEVER use accent lines under titles** — these are a hallmark of AI-"
"generated slides; use whitespace or background color instead"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/powerpoint_SKILL.md:141
msgid "QA (Required)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/powerpoint_SKILL.md:143
msgid "**Assume there are problems. Your job is to find them.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/powerpoint_SKILL.md:145
msgid ""
"Your first render is almost never correct. Approach QA as a bug hunt, not"
" a confirmation step. If you found zero issues on first inspection, you "
"weren't looking hard enough."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/powerpoint_SKILL.md:147
msgid "Content QA"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/powerpoint_SKILL.md:153
msgid "Check for missing content, typos, wrong order."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/powerpoint_SKILL.md:155
msgid "**When using templates, check for leftover placeholder text:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/powerpoint_SKILL.md:161
msgid "If grep returns results, fix them before declaring success."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/powerpoint_SKILL.md:163
msgid "Visual QA"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/powerpoint_SKILL.md:165
msgid ""
"**⚠️ USE SUBAGENTS** — even for 2-3 slides. You've been staring at the "
"code and will see what you expect, not what's there. Subagents have fresh"
" eyes."
msgstr ""

